1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,667
At an automaker, buying one part takes two weeks.

2
00:00:06,667 --> 00:00:13,333
Not because of the supplier: quotes come back in five formats, someone types a comparison into the purchasing system, and the signatures go back and forth between purchase and finance.

3
00:00:13,333 --> 00:00:20,000
Mandi runs that back-and-forth in team chat, on Switch.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:27,500
An engineer asks in chat.

5
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:35,000
Mandi's intake agent turns it into a precise spec.

6
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:42,500
Each supplier gets a sealed, private Switch room.

7
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:50,000
Suppliers who only email a PDF work too; those who opt in bring their own AI sales agent, owned by them.

8
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:56,667
The cheapest quote hides a 50,000-piece minimum on page 2.

9
00:00:56,667 --> 00:01:03,333
Another expired last week.

10
00:01:03,333 --> 00:01:10,000
Mandi catches both, with the exact line.

11
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:17,500
This supplier hid instructions for our AI inside its PDF.

12
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:25,000
Mandi blocks it and disqualifies them.

13
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:33,333
Agents haggle in parallel, citing only offers Mandi has verified.

14
00:01:33,333 --> 00:01:41,667
When Deccan's agent is asked to go below its limit, it asks its own human.

15
00:01:41,667 --> 00:01:50,000
She says no.

16
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:57,500
Now the signatures.

17
00:01:57,500 --> 00:02:05,000
Each gate agent's money tool is a Claude Code tool that must ask permission.

18
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:12,500
Switch relays that request into the room, lets only Meera, or only Vikram, answer it, and records who did.

19
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:20,000
Then Mandi's code checks every rule again.

20
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Anyone else who tries is refused, in the room, for everyone to see.

21
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:34,000
SAP stays the system of record.

22
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Mandi ends with a mock export shaped like an SAP purchase order, so nobody retypes the deal.

23
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:42,000
It's a mock, not an integration, and the fields still need checking by procurement.

24
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:46,333
Minutes, not days.

25
00:02:46,333 --> 00:02:50,667
Sixty-two thousand rupees saved.

26
00:02:50,667 --> 00:02:55,000
Every step recorded in the room.

27
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:56,250
Agents negotiate.

28
00:02:56,250 --> 00:02:57,500
Humans decide.

29
00:02:57,500 --> 00:02:58,750
Switch records who said yes.

30
00:02:58,750 --> 00:03:00,000
— Mandi.
